  "steps": [
    "Dry-roast the peanuts, sesame seeds and coconut separately until fragrant, then grind them coarsely with the onion.",
    "Mix the ground masala with goda masala, chilli powder, turmeric, jaggery, tamarind pulp, salt and coriander leaves.",
    "Stuff each slit brinjal generously with this filling and keep any leftover filling aside.",
    "Heat the oil in a wide pan, crackle the mustard seeds, then add hing and curry leaves.",
    "Arrange the stuffed brinjals in the pan, sprinkle the leftover masala over them and sauté for 3-4 minutes.",
    "Add the water, cover and cook on low heat for 15-20 minutes, turning once, until the brinjals are soft.",
    "Cook uncovered for 2 minutes to thicken the gravy and garnish with coriander."
  ]
}
